    "result": "I added the enterprise plan, and all four plans now live in one table in `account.go`. I could not run the tests because both `go test` calls were denied, so nothing is checked yet.\n\n- **Account:** `IsPro` and `IsTeam` are gone. `Account` now has private `plan` and `seats` fields, so `NewAccount` is the only way to build one. This breaks any outside code that sets `IsPro`/`IsTeam` directly.\n- **Reads:** `MaxProjects`, `MaxStorageGB`, `HasSSO`, `PrioritySupport` and `MonthlyPrice` each return one value from the table. I added `Plan()` and `Seats()` so callers can read those two values.\n- **Prices:** every plan's price is cents per seat times seats. Pro keeps its 1200 because it always has exactly 1 seat.\n- **Tests:** I added `account_test.go` with the limits of all four plans and the `ErrPlan`/`ErrSeats` cases. Run `go test ./...` to check.",
